<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>❄️ LIVE SNOW COVERAGE</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>❄️ LIVE SNOW COVERAGE</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/snow_coverage/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>Snow depth on the ground (in), continuous: <b>LOWEST 0</b> (silver-gray) → <b>HIGHEST+ 24</b> (white extreme). Shows snow currently on the ground. Falling snow, clouds, precipitation without confirmed ground snow, and uncertain observations are transparent.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3 km snow analysis (SNOD snow depth + SNOWC snow cover), hourly cycles).<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-26 04:00 PM EDT<br/><b>Source version:</b> hrrr-hrrr.20260926-t20z<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (analysis)</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>❄️ LIVE SNOW COVERAGE — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Snow_Coverage.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>3600</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
